<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:42:27Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Tunisia: Judge orders arrest of journalist Mohamed Yousfi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:885fd55030591c13b4f9fcba6f6869e91f32a8d909e98196711a995dec7dfcd2</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:42:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T03:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tunisia-judge-orders-arrest-of-journalist-mohamed-yousfi/a-79040802--82239c998f8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tunisia-judge-orders-arrest-of-journalist-mohamed-yousfi/a-79040802?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A journalist and vocal critic of the Tunisian president, Mohamed Yousfi has been taken into custody ahead of an interview. A union called the arrest an attack on all journalists' rights.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bolivia: Deadly explosion rocks military base in Viacha</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e41e5227e7963d94b61337ec03f40f58161d87fa9e9eb40a102974cd42d41544</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:42:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T03:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bolivia-deadly-explosion-rocks-military-base-in-viacha/a-79040892--1c8fa604af29.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bolivia-deadly-explosion-rocks-military-base-in-viacha/a-79040892?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The explosion occurred at an army base where fireworks were stored. The exact cause of the blast is under investigation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys to visit Russia, Ukraine with plan 'to end war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90649e75d63eb2ade47d6fd0ac2aa193e0c774c8ba68f994b211fd36f9e61ad3</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:42:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T01:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-to-visit-russia-ukraine-with-plan-to-end-war/a-79040773--c614556b8611.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-to-visit-russia-ukraine-with-plan-to-end-war/a-79040773?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jared Kushner and Steve Witkoff are set to travel to Russia and Ukraine to revive peace talks. The trip would be the pair's first visit to Kyiv since US President Donald Trump's reelection.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UN approves world map reflecting true size of Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f5fcd5d354e093da9d8d7bf04cf63533451664f0d4f87e17447270de6854854</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:42:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T23:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/un-approves-world-map-reflecting-true-size-of-africa/a-79040629--667e1c8751df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/un-approves-world-map-reflecting-true-size-of-africa/a-79040629?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UN General Assembly voted to adopt a map that more accurately shows the size of the continents. Only the United States voted against the measure, which projects the country as smaller than on traditional maps.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Outrage as Maltese tycoon acquitted in journalist's murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5850e77b18851f855d0836245c8b5ed803ccd269d47f8e15578ed6b03ea5475e</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:42:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008--abbddfce78d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Maltese businessman Yorgen Fenech has been found not guilty of complicity to murder journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia. Almost nine years after the attack, the question of who ordered her death remains unanswered.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Fighting intensifies amid Houthi push in the west</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff1b170c8e98f87de9fab1479c6328a2706b28f14ee9d24aac00bce94e7f2512</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:42:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-fighting-intensifies-amid-houthi-push-in-the-west/a-79039588--c3e077c220f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-fighting-intensifies-amid-houthi-push-in-the-west/a-79039588?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Houthi forces are trying to secure high ground and solidify their control of the entry to the Red Sea in the southwest. The Iran-backed militia abandoned a shaky truce with the Saudi-backed government-in-exile in July.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Small parties will be the kingmakers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84480ff3443bbb7a78d8c83b7cc90e8082544d1b4ce2b8815e1239c67729ba61</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:42:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-small-parties-will-be-the-kingmakers/a-78482460--013f855da7c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-small-parties-will-be-the-kingmakers/a-78482460?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD has good odds of winning an absolute majority in Saxony-Anhalt's parliament this state election, enabling them to govern alone. It all depends on whether other parties make the cut.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's alliance against the far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:717be9a098059287e1237dcde3cea7346db6afb3d1d0d0e52eaaf729006fca06</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alliance-against-the-far-right/a-79009105--a970536f8887.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alliance-against-the-far-right/a-79009105?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trade unions, churches and human rights activists are worried about the rise of the far-right AfD. How can civil society protect people who are threatened by far-right extremism?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria: Suspected oil thieves dead after inhaling fumes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57b495e24e3482dbdabcf7eb0fffd6b7c6a2e138eaa9766f171b2c241630c173</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-suspected-oil-thieves-dead-after-inhaling-fumes/a-79001997--a6ff73c40753.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-suspected-oil-thieves-dead-after-inhaling-fumes/a-79001997?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Nigerian environmental group says that at least 37 people died trying to siphon crude oil off a ship illegally. Police acknowledged a fatal incident but gave fewer details, saying investigations continued.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, partners aim to finalize 'return hubs' by year end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8b4d832de88c5d63ea5eb1c9c2142a455ad44e5b330e9b3ba6a13badedca586</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:42Z</upda